## Creating maps

Anyone can create a map — no key needed. Check a draft first, then store it:

```graphql
mutation { validateMap(map: {id: "my_map", name: "My Map", layout: [">...", "..#*", "...."]}) { valid issues { message } unreachableTreats { x y } } }
```

```graphql
mutation { createMap(map: {id: "my_map", name: "My Map", layout: [">...", "..#*", "...."], mainTapeLength: 8, subTapeLengths: [4], maxSteps: 200}) { id name builtin } }
```

- `id` is the stable handle (`^[a-z0-9_-]{1,64}$`) and must be unused: creating over an id
  that already exists is `INVALID_ARGUMENT`. Use a distinctive prefix.
- The layout needs exactly one start glyph (`^ > v <`), at least one treat (`*`), equal-width rows,
  3–32 cells per side. Up to 10 sub tapes. Tiles are optional: a door letter needs a matching key
  letter, and each portal digit must appear exactly twice, or the map is rejected.
- Defaults: main tape 10, subs `[10]`, max steps 200, max call depth 16, recursion off.
  `subTapeLengths: []` means no subs (different from omitting it).
- `updateMap` and `deleteMap` work on the map you created. Maps with `builtin: true` ship with
  the game and need an `X-Admin-Key` header to change; see provenance with `maps { id builtin }`.
- Play your map like any other: `createSession(mapID: "my_map")`.

